==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn after 3 seconds<sup>90f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycat]] spawns.
*1 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycat]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycat]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycat]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycats]] spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lollycat (Enemy)|Lollycat]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Minimize the amount of Lollycats on screen. One or two is hardly threatening, and meatshields can stall it, but anymore and you will struggle. As such, do not try and rush the stage, as the Lollycat from base hit acts as a sort of anti-cheese, essentially guaranteeing one is going to spawn in addition to the ones already on screen. Once you've beaten 4 Lollycats, then you can hit the base. In addition, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|C. Bahamut]] can often tank for long enough for a single shot, provided only 2 are present. If you have [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker]] cat, this stage becomes laughably easy, as you can just stall as Hacker obliterates everything.

